{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8b0c50c736686a6886ae1de5a5cb4907fb7ff23cc047fecab1617b8c06ec74eb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"sudo-tee/opencode.nvim@636a26425227 snapshot 166e3c2d123d18b6","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a1144807cf1034d796851e80e78d8232ed9f30000bb020461bdd7bc813cd40f3","slc_c3c28a3905436d225dff020f7d7f6213c8ffbee7219f1e7d709524f8c3791077"],"source_ids":["src_a2bbf80420c95f7ca096a720cb368939"],"text":"The model picker sorts favorites first (by favoriting order), then recently used models, then others alphabetically; variant selection per model is remembered for future use.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8f8a01e5f8290537cb72641aee6f97caf91a4521a0d43f7c73e98c246df5bab6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"sudo-tee/opencode.nvim@636a26425227 snapshot 166e3c2d123d18b6","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_68afdba8c732452877a6cb0812eb8813a8d6e5b5f8ff54c0ef8796c5b86803bb"],"source_ids":["src_a2bbf80420c95f7ca096a720cb368939"],"text":"The server configuration supports custom/external opencode servers with url, port, timeout, spawn_command, auto_kill, path_map, and Basic-auth username/password with env-var fallbacks.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8fe2647361b7676fdf1eab07e073f1c931dc290c5f4773295045f7a0faf0f656","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"sudo-tee/opencode.nvim@636a26425227 snapshot 166e3c2d123d18b6","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_729ca0bbb1e2547ed11118b05a2ee0b6c7f77591a5ca1f70ecd3c9067583654a","slc_ae030a1939e79cb76210f85c24e961dcb859cebc26528387b7c67623a8d73d14"],"source_ids":["src_a2bbf80420c95f7ca096a720cb368939"],"text":"Editor context is automatically captured for conversations, including current file, visual selection, mentioned files, diagnostics, and cursor position/line content.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_99fb369f209c07d12b7b1ee9e4962c6f4328c5fd2be596fe0055f682510ba296","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"sudo-tee/opencode.nvim@636a26425227 snapshot 166e3c2d123d18b6","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3dc6bb7739a1daf223f239485c910b8fa403fa0f321ccba4403eb01659b43ed3","slc_c6f6d52723d6cd5da756e56f0a2980330c786ad3e44e7b56293101e6c3b4f417","slc_e7a4ed7d761c0670ade8cb1c61a157fe36baa02a9b9a3bd9dd50fe253e1d2123"],"source_ids":["src_3a0469724adf5ce2a91cf8903773862e"],"text":"Repository development practice: recipe contributions should use the provided template, start from the problem being solved, include a GIF demo, give step-by-step setup instructions, cross-reference related recipes, and be self-contained.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9dfbb7ff2f78e3f6ff3295ed494798bf0e0d7727197d55f2a9432624c6574eba","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"sudo-tee/opencode.nvim@636a26425227 snapshot 166e3c2d123d18b6","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3eb0b1ac6499346667244612218bf6c166a657e747bf8bba7bba3ccbff07b8a4"],"source_ids":["src_a2bbf80420c95f7ca096a720cb368939"],"text":"The plugin bridges Neovim and the opencode AI agent, providing a chat interface that captures editor context such as the current file and selections, with persistent sessions tied to the workspace.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a82290514b057ff325c8033eb9f424dff77f5beeb654cfe8cc9aabefb63f2d42","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"sudo-tee/opencode.nvim@636a26425227 snapshot 166e3c2d123d18b6","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5fc0a4f8b130f764b1757e806c6d4d900fceb91a34c50350673c0b0670211f24","slc_825240406a22561e09d16756e447a42745d93a9dcbdd89a04f54b68737e08472","slc_bcd249eee274f840d04738538b1cf55d5ac06912506b1de9c5b64633d0ef9718"],"source_ids":["src_d6d33359706c5c2ab71ac78ee9ad846e"],"text":"A bidirectional-sync recipe shares one HTTP server (default port 4096) between the opencode TUI and the nvim plugin so session state persists across switches; the TUI attaches via 'opencode attach' and the server stays alive until manually killed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c20d380087d31052ea4c799747cad3915c374858eac35b41fb2316bc65e94a42","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"sudo-tee/opencode.nvim@636a26425227 snapshot 166e3c2d123d18b6","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_55620c9fcb77bd02040211d77e8e92e5a047d941edd89e308f2ffd2ef733cbc0"],"source_ids":["src_99cceb9d93a45636a0c171b4914f01d6"],"text":"The plugin exposes a diff view of modified files since the last prompt via :Opencode diff_open, :Opencode diff open, pressing D on a 'Created Snapshot' output, or the default <leader>od keymap.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d5621af849e40a0dd4d13787851b4189f0188804f6085142a3652b2004c20a61","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"sudo-tee/opencode.nvim@636a26425227 snapshot 166e3c2d123d18b6","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8523b5e2afecc9d49750ab2125c0b83b2f874c1013c23140ac93ff8393adf3d6","slc_901b52b3ba6a478b3f3a6ce4be271da0fb8118f4432e602a7e9426c35f0a38a2"],"source_ids":["src_a2bbf80420c95f7ca096a720cb368939"],"text":"Actions are reachable via default keymaps (e.g. <leader>og toggle), user commands (e.g. :Opencode open input), and Lua API functions such as require('opencode.api').toggle().","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_705275a69d2d4ab6903bf4ce6c686445"}
